  "body": "# Problem\nThe login page currently uses a browser `alert()` for error messages and has no client-side validation for email format or password length. This provides a poor user experience and lacks proper error feedback.\n# Current Behavior\n- No email format validation before submission\n- No password length check\n- Uses `alert()` popup for errors instead of inline error messages\n- No loading state during authentication\n- No accessibility attributes on form fields\n# Proposed Improvement\n- Add email format validation with regex\n- Add minimum password length validation (6 chars)\n- Replace `alert()` with inline error banners\n- Add loading spinner during authentication\n- Add ARIA attributes for screen readers\n- Add `aria-invalid` and error descriptions on inputs\n# Expected Result\nUsers will see clear, inline error messages with proper visual feedback, loading states, and the form will be accessible to screen readers.",
